  "key_evidence": [
    "Why it matters: the government that is supposed to house people demolished their homes. The Lagos State Government cleared waterfront settlements including Makoko, destroying more than 3,000 homes, schools and clinics and displacing about 10,000 people between December 2025 and February 2026.",
    "United Nations human-rights experts publicly condemned the demolitions in February 2026. Residents reported deaths during the clearances, including a newborn.",
    "ATTRIBUTION CORRECTION: the scanner flagged Lagos on the 5 August 2026 protest dispersed with tear gas. Policing in Nigeria is a FEDERAL function; the Nigeria Police Force does not report to Lagos State. That dispersal is NOT scored as the city entity's conduct. The demolitions are.",
    "Lagos then stopped, and that is scored. On 3 February 2026 the state suspended the demolitions and agreed to work with UN agencies on assistance and durable solutions. AB2 scores 3 of 5, the highest Accountability subdimension.",
    "Health provision is real but conditional: 1,502,994 residents enrolled in the Ilera Eko scheme by May 2026, more than half women, alongside a public statement tying access to government services to insurance enrolment."
